serial: resume a stalled backend when FCR resets the receive FIFO

serial_can_receive() reports no room while RBR holds a byte (FIFO off)
or the FIFO is full, and the chardev backend then stops polling until
the frontend calls qemu_chr_fe_accept_input().  Reading RBR does that;
an FCR write with RFR -- which empties the FIFO and clears DR -- did
not.  Input that arrived before a guest initialised its UART (one byte
in RBR, FIFO off) therefore stalled the line for good if the guest's
next step was a FIFO reset and its input check reads only LSR, as
U-Boot's ns16550 tstc() does: no further byte was ever delivered, and
"Hit any key to stop autoboot" could not be answered.  Seen with the
Novatek NT9856x vendor U-Boot 2019.04 (bootdelay 0): keys queued from
power-on reached the guest only once Linux read RBR.

---
diff --git a/hw/char/serial.c b/hw/char/serial.c
index 03fec3f..c2407c2 100644
--- a/hw/char/serial.c
+++ b/hw/char/serial.c
@@ -417,6 +417,8 @@ static void serial_ioport_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, uint64_t val,
             timer_del(s->fifo_timeout_timer);
             s->timeout_ipending = 0;
             fifo8_reset(&s->recv_fifo);
+            /* Room again: a backend stalled on a full RBR / FIFO resumes. */
+            qemu_chr_fe_accept_input(&s->chr);
         }
 
         if (val & UART_FCR_XFR) {
